        "text": "No same-side rule. Apex's rule restricts identical entries across multiple Apex accounts. TPT's tightening on copy-trading is similar in spirit but enforced through a different consistency-tracking mechanism at payout review, not as a hard intraday block. PMT manages this with smart per-account routing rules."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is automated trading allowed at TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Personal automation - your own TradingView strategies, your own NinjaTrader indicators, your own Python or scripts - is fully allowed on both Challenge and PRO. PickMyTrade is the dominant TradingView-to-Tradovate automation bridge for TPT users at $50/month per broker connection across all your TPT accounts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are commercial bots and EAs permitted?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Mass-distributed commercial bots, paid-signal-service EAs, and group-shared algorithms are prohibited. The reasoning: TPT can't fund the same strategy across hundreds of accounts because the firm bears net risk on the cumulative book. Personal proprietary scripts you wrote yourself are fine."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does TPT consider \"copy trading\"?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Two specific patterns: (1) identical fills across multiple TPT accounts (your own or others'), (2) following a signal-service master account where multiple strangers receive the same trades. TPT tightened both throughout 2024-2025. The risk system flags suspiciously aligned timestamps and identical order parameters across accounts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Did TPT recently tighten copy-trade rules?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Through 2024-2025, TPT publicly tightened multi-account copy-trade enforcement. New language in the funded trader agreement explicitly bars cross-account replication. Cap on simultaneous funded accounts per identity dropped from \"unlimited\" to a 3-5 functional cap. This was an industry-wide trend (Apex did the same)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I run the same TradingView strategy on TPT and Apex?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - across different firms is generally permitted. The copy-trade restriction applies within TPT (multiple TPT accounts), not across firms. PMT lets one TradingView alert broadcast to TPT, Apex, MFFU, Topstep, and Bulenox simultaneously - a common multi-firm strategy. Each firm sees only its own account's fills."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does PMT trigger TPT's copy-trade detection?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If you run a single PMT account routing to one TPT PRO, no - that's standard automation, identical to placing trades manually. The risk emerges only when you mirror identical fills across multiple TPT PROs. PMT supports per-account jitter (random 200-500ms timing offsets, slight contract variations) to differentiate fills if you must run multiple TPT accounts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are signal services allowed on TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Subscribing to signal services and acting on them manually is permitted. Direct mass-broadcast where the same signal hits dozens of TPT accounts in milliseconds is the violation. If a signal service publishes a setup and you choose to enter, that's discretion. If a bot mirrors fills automatically, that's the prohibited copy pattern."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does PMT support TPT-specific automation safeguards?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. PickMyTrade has TPT-aware features: per-account contract caps matching the 3/6/9/12/15-mini limits, Trading Time active hours to automatically reject alerts outside your configured window (preventing trades after TPT's EOD cutoff), custom intraday drawdown halts, and weekly P&L distribution smoothing for the consistency check. Configured once, applied to every TradingView webhook."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is TradingView Pine Script automation allowed?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Pine Script strategies running on TradingView and firing webhooks via PMT to your TPT Tradovate account are fully allowed. This is the most common TPT automation setup. PickMyTrade processes the webhook, validates per-account risk rules, and submits the order to Tradovate FCM connected to TPT."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the safest automation pattern on TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Single TPT PRO Account, your own proprietary TradingView strategy, PMT routing webhooks to Tradovate, Trading Time active hours configured to end before TPT's EOD cutoff. PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections — you can configure active trading hours and any alerts outside those hours are automatically rejected. You can set your trading window to end before TPT's EOD cutoff, preventing any new trades from being placed after that time. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What trading platforms does TPT support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Three: NinjaTrader (with NT Continuum data), Tradovate (web/desktop), and TradingView via Tradovate connectivity. You pick one platform when activating PRO and can switch with a request to support. Tradovate is the most popular for TradingView automation users; NinjaTrader is preferred by chart-heavy discretionary traders."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does TPT use Rithmic data?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Currently no - Rithmic is not natively supported. TPT runs on NinjaTrader Continuum (separate from Rithmic) and Tradovate's own infrastructure. If you need Rithmic for a specific platform, look at Apex, Topstep, or MyFundedFutures, which offer Rithmic connectivity. PMT supports Rithmic on the firms that use it."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use TradingView directly with TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - through Tradovate's broker integration in TradingView. TradingView connects to your TPT-issued Tradovate credentials, displaying TPT account data and accepting orders directly from the chart. Pine Script alerts - webhooks - PMT - Tradovate API - TPT account is the most-used automation flow."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does TPT charge platform fees?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradovate web/desktop is free for TPT customers. NinjaTrader requires a license (Lifetime $,099 or Lease ~$60/month) for advanced features; the free version supports TPT Sim accounts but with charting limitations. TradingView's premium tiers ($4-$60/month) unlock more concurrent webhooks if needed."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which platform is best for automated trading at TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradovate via TradingView + PickMyTrade. The webhook flow has low latency (typically under 500ms end-to-end), runs on cloud-hosted PMT infrastructure (no local PC dependency), and supports multi-firm broadcasting. NinjaTrader supports automation natively but requires a local PC running 24/7 - less reliable for set-and-forget systems."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use NinjaScript bots at TPT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - NinjaTrader's native NinjaScript automation runs on TPT NT Continuum accounts. Personal NinjaScript strategies (your own code) are permitted. Mass-distributed NT8 paid bots are subject to the same commercial-bot prohibition. PMT does not directly route to NinjaTrader; for NT users, the platform's own automation is the recommended path."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does TPT support mobile trading?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - Tradovate has iOS and Android apps with full order entry, position monitoring, and chart access. NinjaTrader Mobile is more limited. TradingView mobile app supports order entry to Tradovate. Most disciplined PRO traders avoid mobile-only execution because the trailing drawdown punishes mistimed taps."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the latency of PMT webhooks to TPT Tradovate?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Median end-to-end (TradingView fire - PMT process - Tradovate fill confirmation) is 300-700ms. PMT runs cloud infrastructure colocated near major exchange data centers. For most discretionary and swing automation strategies this is fast enough; ultra-HFT styles aren't TPT-permitted anyway."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I switch platforms mid-account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Submit a support ticket to switch from NinjaTrader to Tradovate or vice versa. Account history transfers; only the platform UI changes. Often takes 24-48 hours to provision new credentials. Some traders switch from NT to Tradovate specifically to add TradingView/PMT automation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I connect PMT to my TPT Tradovate account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Go to pickmytrade.trade, add Tradovate as your broker connection, and authenticate with your TPT-issued Tradovate credentials. Then use Generate Alert to get your JSON configuration and webhook URL. Paste the webhook URL into your TradingView alert and the JSON into the alert message. PMT validates the connection in 2-3 minutes. Full setup guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.trade/docs/automating-tradingview-strategies-with-pickmytrade/"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does a Test phase reset cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "$00 flat for any Test phase size, AND one free reset is included with each monthly subscription renewal. Reset clears the failed trailing drawdown, sets your balance back to starting capital, and you continue under the existing monthly subscription. Cheaper than purchasing a new Test. PRO resets are separate (size-scaled, $449-$,499, max 3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How many times can I reset the Test or PRO?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Test phase: unlimited paid resets at $00 flat, plus one free reset with each monthly renewal. PRO: up to 3 paid resets per account, with size-scaled fees from roughly $449 (smaller sizes) to $,499 (larger sizes). PRO+ live brokerage accounts cannot typically be reset - breaches are terminal and you’d need to repurchase a Test."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does TPT offer refunds?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Subscription fees are non-refundable once the Test phase starts trading. The PRO Account activation fee is non-refundable once paid. Reset fees are non-refundable. Cancellation simply stops future renewal charges. TPT does occasionally honor refund requests for technical glitches caused on their side; submit a support ticket with documentation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I cancel my TPT subscription anytime?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Log into the dashboard, go to billing, click cancel. The active month continues until the renewal date; no new charge after that. You retain access through the current billing cycle. PRO and PRO+ accounts don't have a subscription - they only require trading activity to remain active."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens if I let my Test subscription lapse?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The Test phase account closes when the subscription expires. Any progress (current balance, trailing drawdown level, days traded toward the 5-day minimum) is lost. To resume, purchase a fresh Test - old progress does not carry forward. Always renew or cancel intentionally; don't let it lapse mid-pass."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I pause my Test phase?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No formal pause feature. Cancel and resubscribe later if needed, but progress resets. The closest thing to \"pause\" is to simply stop trading - your account remains active without orders. The trailing drawdown won't move because there's no activity, so you can step away for days or weeks within an active billing month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens to my PRO Account if I stop trading?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PRO and PRO+ accounts have a minimum activity expectation: typically one trade every 30 days. Beyond that, the account may be marked inactive and closed. If closed, accumulated unrequested profits are forfeited. Always request payouts before extended absences and place at least one small trade per month to maintain status."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "If I fail PRO, can I get a discount on my next Test?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sometimes - TPT runs occasional \"comeback\" promotions for previously funded traders, with discount codes ranging from 25% to 50% off the next Test phase. Check email for re-engagement offers. There's no guaranteed reduced-price re-entry; pricing reverts to standard list/promo for new Test purchases."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Take Profit Trader vs Apex Trader Funding - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TPT wins on payout cadence (on-demand vs Apex 8-day) and uniquely offers PRO+ - a real LIVE Tradovate brokerage tier with a flat 90/10 split. Apex wins on size variety (up to $300K), instant funded option, and looser copy-trade rules historically. PRO at TPT pays a flat 80/20; PRO+ flat 90/10. Pick TPT for live-execution upgrade path; Apex for larger sim sizes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Take Profit Trader vs Topstep - which is better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Topstep enforces a Max Loss Limit per day; TPT does not. Topstep pays monthly; TPT pays on-demand. Topstep is the OG (founded 2012) with the strongest brand and broadest education. TPT’s 3-tier model (Test - PRO sim - PRO+ live) is unique among major US futures props. Pick Topstep for structured risk safeguards and education; TPT for on-demand payouts and the live-brokerage upgrade."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Take Profit Trader vs MyFundedFutures (MFFU)?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU offers more plan variety (Core, Rapid, Pro, Builder, Flex) and bigger sizes (up to $300K). TPT is simpler - one Test phase, five sizes, plus PRO and PRO+ tiers. MFFU’s static drawdown option is friendlier than TPT’s intraday trailing on PRO. TPT’s PRO+ live-brokerage tier (flat 90/10) is something MFFU does not offer. TPT for the live upgrade path; MFFU for plan variety."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Take Profit Trader vs Bulenox?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bulenox runs aggressive 1-step like TPT but with looser trailing drawdowns and a simpler split (90% from dollar one on funded). Bulenox uses Rithmic (not Tradovate) — different platform stack from TPT. Many multi-firm traders run Bulenox alongside TPT to diversify. Bulenox does not offer a live-brokerage tier - TPT’s PRO+ is unique in that regard."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "TPT vs FundedNext for futures?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "FundedNext is primarily forex with a smaller futures arm. TPT is futures-only and more mature in the futures vertical. For pure futures traders, TPT is the better fit. For traders mixing forex and futures, FundedNext or E8 Markets makes more sense. Don't pick FundedNext for futures-only - TPT's product is more refined for the asset class."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Should I run TPT alongside other prop firms with PMT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - multi-firm broadcasting is the most common advanced PMT use case. One TradingView Pine strategy fires a single webhook; PMT routes copies to TPT, Apex, MFFU, Topstep, and Bulenox simultaneously. Diversifies firm-specific risk (rule changes, outages, account closures). Single $50/month per broker connection covers every connected firm including TPT’s PRO+ live brokerage."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is TPT cheaper than Apex over a 6-month period?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Depends on pass speed. TPT's monthly Test subscription means each month adds cost; Apex charges one eval fee then monthly funded fee. If you pass TPT in 1 month and quickly graduate to PRO and PRO+ (no recurring fee), TPT is cheaper. If it takes 4-6 months on the Test phase, Apex's structure starts to win. Promo codes affect both. Math out per-pass cost based on your historical timeline."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the multi-firm playbook on PMT?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Common stack: 1 TPT 50 (Test - PRO - PRO+), 1 Apex 50K, 1 MFFU 50K, 1 Topstep 50K. Same TradingView Pine strategy, single webhook, PMT broadcasts. ~$,000/month combined Test/eval subscription cost while in evaluation; potential combined on-demand payouts of $,500-$3,000 once all four funded accounts are active. Diversifies firm-specific failure modes. Don't run identical fills across the same firm - that's the copy-trade violation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I owe taxes on TPT profits?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - taxable income wherever you live. TPT issues a 1099-NEC for US traders (self-employment income on PRO; live brokerage income on PRO+). International traders receive payment statements via PayPal/Wise/Plaid. UK: HMRC self-employment. India: ITR-3 business income. EU: per-country trading income. Consult a local tax professional."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where can I see TPT payout proof?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TPT's official X (Twitter), Discord, YouTube channel, plus payout-proof posts on prop firm forums, futures trader forums, and day trader forums. Trustpilot has roughly 8,751 reviews referencing payouts at ~4.4/5. Cross-reference firm-published numbers with community user reports for the truest picture. PMT users frequently share on-demand payout receipts from both PRO and PRO+ accounts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade TPT on a VPS?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. NinjaTrader on a Windows VPS is permitted and common for traders running NinjaScript automation 24/7. Tradovate runs in-browser, also VPS-compatible. PickMyTrade is cloud-hosted, eliminating the VPS need for TradingView automation users - webhooks fire from PMT's infrastructure even when your local PC is off."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "TPT vs TickTickTrader - which suits algo traders better?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TickTickTrader is newer with explicit algo-friendly messaging and ProjectX/Tradovate platform support. TPT has more brand maturity and on-demand payouts that beat TickTick’s 14-day cycle. For automation-first traders, both work via PMT. TPT’s PRO uses an intraday trailing drawdown that’s stricter than TickTick’s static-drawdown options, but TPT’s PRO+ live brokerage tier is something TickTick does not offer. Most multi-firm PMT users run both side by side."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Final pick - should I start with TPT in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "If you want a 1-step Test, on-demand payouts, no daily loss limit, and the unique option to graduate to a real LIVE Tradovate brokerage (PRO+ at 90/10) - yes, TPT is one of the best options. Pair it with PickMyTrade for TradingView automation and you’re set up for $50/month per broker connection across TPT and any future firm additions. Start at TPT 50, learn the Test rules, push toward PRO and PRO+."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I set trading time restrictions in PickMyTrade for my TPT account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections. You can configure specific active trading windows with start and end times (24-hour ET format). Any TradingView alerts received outside your configured hours are automatically rejected — no new trades are placed. Existing open positions remain active. Settings can be applied to specific accounts or all accounts at once. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/ For Tradovate connections, PickMyTrade also integrates with ForexFactory to automatically pause trading before and after scheduled news events — it can close open positions and cancel pending limit/stop orders during news windows. Tradovate Trading Time guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.trade/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
